2026-09-03T05:23Z claude note Filed by the ripple lane against origin/main 5282918. The design in the body is the author's as he settled it on 2026-09-03, not this lane's proposal: rows driven from README.md's ladder roster rather than from the artifacts, grouped by goal then requirement, a KEPT? row per group per column under the fixed precedence fail > no-test > not-run > not-offered, four kinds of cell with no-test among them, interface-only so fold_sweep.mjs is out of the matrix, seats with no artifact named rather than omitted, and the whole thing generated with a regeneration check so a stale table is a red build. The starting data was re-measured here at 8a5ad06 rather than transcribed and every figure reproduced: zoteus 10 checks 4 pass 2 fail 1 not-offered 3 not-run, the other three artifacts 5 checks each, R10-no-egress fail on all four, goal-2 rows only for zoteus, and no committed acceptance.json anywhere for zotero-mcp.
--- body ---

## Context

The ladder's standing report says how each requirement stands. It does not say,
per target, what actually ran. That second picture exists only as four
`acceptance.json` artifacts nobody reads side by side, and the one time it was
assembled by hand — a prototype run on 2026-09-03 — it immediately showed
things no page in this repo says: `R10-no-egress` fails on **all four** executed
targets, goal 2 has rows for exactly one of them, and **zotero-mcp has no
committed `acceptance.json` anywhere** although its adapter merged in pull
request #219.

A hand-written table of that would go stale the first time an artifact
regenerated, and nothing would notice. So the deliverable is a **generated**
matrix, committed, with a regeneration check in this repo's existing figure-guard
pattern, so that a table which no longer matches the artifacts is a red build
rather than a quiet lie.

**The point of the whole thing is the holes.** A matrix built from the artifacts
can only show assertions that exist, which makes a requirement nobody tests
indistinguishable from a requirement nobody has. Rows therefore come from
`README.md`'s ladder roster: every requirement on every rung gets a row,
including goals 3, 4 and 5, whose rows will be almost entirely empty. That is
the honest picture, not a defect in the report.

R19 is the live example of why. On 2026-09-03 its clause was reworded into a
promise about what a user sees, its standing row went to `none` / `inferred`,
and no assertion of the new shape exists (ticket 0603). Under a matrix built
from artifacts, R19 would simply be absent. Under this one it is a row of
`no test` across every column, which is what a reader needs to see.

## Relevant files

- `README.md`, "## The goals ladder" — the row set. Five goals, each a roster
  of requirements, one requirement per rung.
- `bench/check_progress.py` — **reuse its parse, do not write a second one.**
  `goal_split`, `goal_members` and `ruled_members` already read the roster and
  already fail the build when a requirement sits on none or two rungs.
- `bench/check_figures.py` — the pattern the regeneration check follows: a
  committed artifact, a checker that recomputes and compares, and a ratchet
  whose slack has to be argued (see finding F2 on ticket 0026).
- `bench/acceptance/run.py`, `bench/acceptance/assertions.py`,
  `bench/acceptance/interface.py` — the layer that produces the cells and the
  ratified seven-verb interface that bounds them.
- `bench/acceptance/adapters/` — five ratified targets: `zoteus`, `zotseek`,
  `beaver`, `zotero_core_6012`, `zotero_mcp`.
- The committed artifacts, measured at `8a5ad06`:
  `bench/results/smoke-1.12.0/acceptance-zoteus.json`,
  `bench/results/0586-beaver/acceptance.json`,
  `bench/results/0584-zotseek/acceptance.json`,
  `bench/results/0583-zotero-6012/acceptance.json`. There is no fifth.
- `Makefile` — where `ladder-matrix` and its check are wired.

## The design, as the author settled it

**Rows.** Driven from `README.md`'s ladder roster through
`check_progress.py`'s existing parse — never from the artifacts, and never by a
second parser. Every requirement on every rung gets a row.

**Grouping.** By goal, then by requirement.

**Columns.** One per ratified target.

**Cells.** Four kinds, and conflating any two destroys the artifact's value:

| cell | means | a statement about |
|---|---|---|
| `pass` / `fail` | the assertion ran and decided | the target |
| `not-offered` | the adapter declared the verb absent | the target |
| `not-run` | the assertion ran and could not decide | the run |
| `no test` | no assertion exists for this requirement | **us** |

**A `KEPT?` row per group, per column.** `KEPT` only when every member of that
rung passed for that target. Otherwise `NO:` followed by the worst blocker in
the fixed precedence **fail > no-test > not-run > not-offered**. The precedence
is load-bearing and is not a tie-break convenience: a column blocked by `fail`
is a finding about the target, and a column blocked by `no-test` is a finding
about us. Reporting the second where the first is true would let a target's
failure hide behind our own missing assertion.

**Interface-only.** Every cell is filled by driving the target through the seven
ratified verbs, as a user would. A requirement decidable only by reading source
does not get a cell — which is exactly the criterion the R19 ruling of
2026-09-03 established, and the reason **`fold_sweep.mjs` is out of the
matrix**. No fifth state for it, and no peer column for repo-side gates.

**Seats with no artifact are named, not omitted.** Measured at `8a5ad06`: of
five ratified targets, four have a committed `acceptance.json` and
**zotero-mcp has none anywhere**, though its adapter merged in pull request
#219. A matrix that silently showed four columns would report a roster of four.
The tool must say that the fifth seat exists and never ran.

## Starting data — re-measure it, do not transcribe it

Reproduced in this filing at `8a5ad06`, so an implementer can tell a rebuild
that works from one that does not:

- `acceptance-zoteus.json`: **10** checks — 4 `pass`, 2 `fail`, 1
  `not-offered`, 3 `not-run`.
- `0586-beaver`, `0584-zotseek`, `0583-zotero-6012`: **5** checks each.
- **`R10-no-egress` is `fail` on all four**, verb `query`.
- Goal-2 rows (`R3-edit-recomputes-only-what-changed`,
  `R3-identical-resync-recomputes-nothing`,
  `R13-two-processes-both-answer`,
  `R13-two-processes-do-not-duplicate-work`,
  `R23-foreign-stamp-ends-up-serving`) exist **only** for zoteus, because
  `durability.py` landed after the other three adapters ran.
- Goal 1 is covered for only two of its four terms: R10 and R15 have checks;
  R22 belongs to ticket 0033 and R31 to ticket 0488, neither in this layer. Both
  are `no test` rows, and that is the correct reading.
- Goals 3, 4 and 5: no checks at all.

## Actions

1. Write the generator. Rows from `check_progress.py`'s roster parse; cells from
   the committed `acceptance.json` artifacts, keyed by requirement; `no test`
   wherever the roster names a requirement no registered check has as its
   subject.
2. Emit the `KEPT?` row per group per column with the fixed precedence above.
3. Name every ratified target as a column, including one with no artifact, and
   make the absence legible as an absence rather than as a row of blanks that
   could be read as `not-offered`.
4. Commit the rendered table and add `make ladder-matrix`. Add the regeneration
   check to `check` in the `check_figures.py` pattern: regenerate, compare,
   fail on any difference.
5. Leave a pointer where the next reader of the acceptance layer will meet it —
   the matrix is the layer's report, and a reader arriving at
   `assertions.py` should be told where the cross-target picture lives.

## Test

**Must be seen red before it is trusted.** A matrix that has never mis-reported
has not been shown to report at all.

- Remove one assertion from a **copy** of an artifact, regenerate, and confirm
  the cell flips to the right state and that the committed-table check fails.
  Both halves matter: a cell that flips while the check stays green means the
  guard is not wired; a check that fails while the cell reads wrong means the
  generator is not.
- Drive the precedence directly: a group whose members include one `fail` and
  one `no test` must report `NO: fail`, and the same group with the `fail`
  removed must report `NO: no-test`. A single fixture cannot show a precedence;
  two that differ in exactly one member can.
- The missing-seat arm: with `zotero-mcp`'s column present and empty, confirm
  its `KEPT?` reads as never-run and not as `KEPT`.

## Verification

- [ ] rows come from `README.md`'s roster via `check_progress.py`'s parse, and
      no second roster parser was written
- [ ] goals 3, 4 and 5 appear with their rows, empty
- [ ] R19 appears as `no test` across every column
- [ ] `fold_sweep.mjs` appears nowhere in the matrix
- [ ] the removed-assertion arm was run and both the cell and the check moved
- [ ] the two precedence fixtures give `NO: fail` and `NO: no-test`
- [ ] `zotero-mcp` is a named column with no artifact
- [ ] `make ladder-matrix` regenerates the committed table byte-identically on
      an unchanged tree
- [ ] `make check` green; `./tickets/erg check tickets/` green

## Invariants

- **The row set is the roster's, never the artifacts'.** The moment rows are
  derived from what ran, the report loses the only thing it was built to show.
- **One parse.** `check_progress.py` already owns the roster; a second parser is
  a second thing to keep in sync and a second thing to be wrong.
- **No number from `SPEC.md` is copied into the table or this ticket.**
- **The four kinds of cell stay four.** Do not collapse `not-run` into `fail`,
  and do not let `not-offered` stand in for a seat that never ran.
- **Interface-only.** No cell is filled by reading a target's source, and no
  repo-side gate gets a column.
- The generator names no target in its logic; column identity comes from the
  adapter roster, so `tests/test_acceptance_layer_is_target_neutral.py`'s spirit
  holds here too.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `make ladder-matrix` exists, generates the matrix, and the rendered table
      is committed
- [ ] a regeneration check runs in `check` and fails on a stale table
- [ ] the matrix carries every requirement of every rung, grouped by goal then
      requirement, with `KEPT?` per group per column under the fixed precedence
- [ ] all four kinds of cell occur in the committed output, `no test` included
- [ ] the fifth seat with no artifact is named
- [ ] the removed-assertion red was run and recorded in this ticket's log
